From 5a867ed6f794e0b94c7b8ae66c5feb45c6adf136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:16:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 053/137] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: Add the CPU capacities and
 dynamic power coefficients

The CPU nodes have no capacity-dmips-mhz, so every core reports a
capacity of 1024: the scheduler treats the Cortex-A55s like the
Cortex-X1, and without dynamic-power-coefficient no energy model is
registered, so energy-aware scheduling stays off.

Take the values the downstream lahaina device tree uses (the same
scheme as sm8250.dtsi): Cortex-A55 1024 / 100, Cortex-A78 1946 / 499,
Cortex-X1 2048 / 760. With the cluster maximum frequencies this gives
the capacities 325, 828 and 1024.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
index 9144bc2243e0..1b3ef745d36d 100644
